Package: battery-manager
Version: 0.1.1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, systemd, polkitd | policykit-1
Maintainer: Sandeep Singh <mailme.sandeepsingh@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/rapsalands/battery-manager
Description: Battery charge cycle manager for ASUS laptops on Linux
 Cycles the laptop battery between configurable low and high percentages
 by dynamically managing charge_control_end_threshold. Works around the
 ASUS firmware quirk of silently ignoring threshold values that sit too
 far below the current capacity, and self-corrects when the firmware
 resets the threshold on AC events.
 .
 Ships with a GTK 3 / AppIndicator tray applet that shows the current
 capacity, phase, and threshold, lets you toggle the daemon on/off, and
 exposes a small settings dialog for adjusting the low / high values.
